From e26afaf76438c52e774afc32b2d3354af6edc588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:00:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bound effect-duration lookups to the duration table

game_actor_launch_effect accepts effect IDs up to 60000, and
rag_effect_init reads g_effectDurations[effect_id] for every one, but
the table has 2,385 rows. A server effect ID from 2385 to 60000 reads
past the end of the table and gives the effect an arbitrary lifetime.
rag_effect_init has no case at or above 2385, so these effects are
inert apart from that lifetime. Lua-listed ground effect IDs in
session_play_ground_skill_effect index the same table without a bound.
The 2022-04-06 executable reads its table the same way.

Add effect_duration(), which returns the table row for IDs inside the
table. Any other ID gets its own value, as the unconfigured rows do:
1,141 of the 2,385 rows, including the last unconfigured ones before
the end, hold their own ID. Use it at both data-driven lookups.

Validation: the new test_effect_launch_duration runs the extracted
rag_effect_init against the real table for IDs inside it, at its end
and up to 60000; it fails without the fix. The existing table checksum
test is unchanged. Release build without warnings; the full behavioral
suite passed on the completed series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
